schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Social Token
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A community-specific token representing membership, access, or
    reputation, whose value derives primarily from its social context
    rather than a stand-alone utility function.
  source_traditions:
    - Community-building practice (per article frontmatter source)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Split into three types for local-node use: creator tokens (audience
    access/governance over a creator's direction), community tokens
    (membership, earned or purchased, used for governance/access/identity),
    and reputation tokens (non-transferable, contribution-history record —
    "a resume on-chain").
  adjacent_meanings:
    - creator token
    - community token
    - reputation token
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Social token vs utility token: a utility token's value comes from a
      defined function; a social token's value comes from the social context
      it exists in.
    - >-
      Reputation tokens are explicitly non-transferable, distinguishing them
      from tradeable creator/community tokens.
  tensions:
    - >-
      Community tokens can be "earned through contribution or purchased" —
      two very different legitimacy models for the same token type,
      unresolved in the source.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "social token" as one category flattens real differences in
    transferability, governance weight, and regulatory exposure between
    creator, community, and reputation tokens.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/social-tokens-creator.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
